{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q82882113","formula":"C₁₆H₂₅NO₂","hill":"C16H25NO2","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":16.0,"H":25.0,"N":1.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"5-Methoxy-N,N-dipropyl-3,4-dihydro-2H-1-benzopyran-3-amine"},"descriptions":{"en":"5-MeO-DPAC, also known as 5-methoxy-3-(dipropylamino)chroman, is a potent and highly selective serotonin 5-HT1A receptor full agonist related to 8-OH-DPAT. It is a derivative of 3-aminochroman, in which in the 5th position of the benzene ring there is a methoxy group, and in the 3rd position of dipropylamine. The drug shows no affinity for other serotonin receptors or for the dopamine D2 receptor. It acts at very low concentrations, albeit with lower potency than 8-OH-DPAT, and unlike 8-OH-DPAT, does not bind to presynaptic serotonin 5-HT1A receptors in the striatum."},"fame":1,"pubchemCid":3082597,"mass":263.37,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCCN(CCC)C1CC2=C(C=CC=C2OC)OC1","inchikey":"GOWYIQOIWRLZLO-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"5-methoxy-N,N-dipropyl-3,4-dihydro-2H-chromen-3-amine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"3082597","atoms":44,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.747,"y":2.296,"z":-0.309,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.704,"y":-2.081,"z":0.398,"el":"O"},{"x":2.07,"y":0.018,"z":0.567,"el":"N"},{"x":0.802,"y":0.416,"z":-0.034,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.319,"y":-0.515,"z":0.429,"el":"C"},{"x":0.442,"y":1.847,"z":0.355,"el":"C"},{"x":3.148,"y":0.906,"z":0.128,"el":"C"},{"x":2.387,"y":-1.371,"z":0.23,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.657,"y":0.057,"z":0.051,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.795,"y":1.412,"z":-0.279,"el":"C"},{"x":4.466,"y":0.506,"z":0.787,"el":"C"},{"x":2.46,"y":-1.544,"z":-1.285,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.793,"y":-0.763,"z":0.056,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.044,"y":1.926,"z":-0.638,"el":"C"},{"x":5.599,"y":1.427,"z":0.364,"el":"C"},{"x":2.767,"y":-2.985,"z":-1.663,"e